+# Unit44 — captured-target ordered import router (pending Actions)
+
+## Upper-contract and policy audit
+
+Continue fully read development-policy.md v0.2.6 and AGENT.md, unchanged. Source45 assets.py importProjectAssetFiles and pseudocode23 application/public_api/assets.pcal ordered router require empty input no effects; one captured Frontend scalar target; official filename/MIME classifier; each input uses exactly one slot/package/directory helper; preserve input order/copied results; stop at cancellation/noncommit/original exception without rolling back earlier files. One public importing lifecycle; UI must not nest another. No new Source meaning or ownership cache.
+
+## Direct translation / bounded prompt-to-artifact checklist
+
+- importProjectAssetFiles captures an ordered file array and selectedSlotId before waits, calls readAssetFileKind per file, passes captured target to importProjectFileToSlot or importSelectedGraphFile, otherwise uses the correct CSV/image directory. No mutable selected-slot snapshot, first-image-only branch, silent CSV-to-image type conversion, Application candidate/create/replace/connect or rollback.
+- Single runLifecycleTask lives in this public operation after empty guard. Mantine caller awaits it and reports error outside task, preserving original lifecycle failure. Empty returns[], cancellation returns None, noncommit returns the exact result, throw propagates, successful output is ordered per-helper detached items.
+- Remove now-unreferenced loadDataFile/loadImageFile/connectDataToSlotModel/connectDataToSlot after all real raw-router callers cut over. No compatibility bridge or duplicate persistent state. Package helper accepts scalar target and copies official chart read, but this does NOT close its older internal parser/caller-chart action.
+- Case120 uses stubbed helpers to isolate routing/captured target across waits, per-kind directories, original-order all-file outputs, empty no-effects, one lifecycle, busy rejection, cancel/noncommit early stop and original exception/lifecycle failure. Package routing in this case is delegation proof ONLY, not parser/Backend conformance.
+- Case121 uses actual corrected raw helpers: multiple images all commit and link in order while preserving settings; CSV into image target noncommits without changing type or processing next file; mixed project imports keep order/directories; later unsupported file leaves earlier actual commit intact. Prior116–119 retain command atomicity/current authority/resource evidence.
+
+## Remaining dependency gaps / no whole closure
+
+Package graph import still parses in Application importSlotFile and sends a chart/CSV model to applySlotChartImportedAction; this violates already-current Source graphs.importSelectedGraphFile raw-file-only/Backend ownership and remains OPEN. Do not infer package conformance from router stubs or prior roundtrip cases. The package wrapper's useful-work/noncommit boundary requires closing with that handler, not another caller-side rollback/temporary model. Inspect Source versus pseudocode target-kind guards before that cutover: Source describes target slot and ApplyFfsx preserves settings, while pseudocode main branch currently names ResolveCurrentVisibleGraphSlot; do not silently impose or remove an upper precondition from code convenience. Current package action also resets imageSettings and lacks current-source retry/canonical extension preservation. These are concrete next audit/implementation tasks, not fixed here.
+
+Common final-commit/initializer semantics, other mutation owners, schema/serializer/raster/current snapshot/resources, supplied dashboard and lifecycle/timing integration and full requirement audit remain open. Code95 stale; optional model/TLC not run. No local app/test/build/checker. All exact new-SHA121 inline+121 split/repeat/build/canonical/cumulative/fidelity PENDING; staged Git blob fingerprint is metadata calculation, not checker pass. No explicit quota/auth/service blocker.
